{"name":"Delselar","status":"ok","title":"Delselar","pageId":123948,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Delselar\" title=\"Category:Maps of Delselar\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Delselar</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-p9-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3.M_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3.M-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"alt spelling\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Alt. spelling</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Dolselar</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"aliases\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Aliases</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">The City of Succulent Jewels</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thindol\" title=\"Thindol\">Thindol</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Chultan_Peninsula\" title=\"Chultan Peninsula\">Chultan Peninsula</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">76,412 in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Human</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Yuan-ti\" title=\"Yuan-ti\">Yuan-ti</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Delselar\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Delselar\">Organizations in  Delselar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"DPL-purge plainlinks\"><a class=\"text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Category_intersection_jump?DPL_cat1=Locations_in__Delselar&amp;DPL_cat2=Bodies_of_water&amp;action=purge\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Bodies of water  in  Delselar</a></span></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Delselar</b>, also known locally as <b>Dolselar</b> and the <b>City of Succulent Jewels</b><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, was a large city found in southern <a href=\"/wiki/Thindol\" title=\"Thindol\">Thindol</a> on the <a href=\"/wiki/Chultan_Peninsula\" title=\"Chultan Peninsula\">Chultan Peninsula</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-p9-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Activities\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Activities</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Rumors_&amp;_Legends\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rumors &amp; Legends</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Delselar was founded on the southern border of the <a href=\"/wiki/Guthland\" title=\"Guthland\">Guthland</a> near the mouth of the <a href=\"/wiki/Thingulph\" title=\"Thingulph\">Thingulph</a> along the southern bank of the <a href=\"/wiki/River_Dolsel\" title=\"River Dolsel\">River Dolsel</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRA-p9-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3.M_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3.M-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Delselar was unwalled, stretching for 3 miles  (4.8 kilometers) along the banks of the river. The vast majority of structures within Delselar were within a stone's throw from the water.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Activities\">Activities</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Activities\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Activities\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Agents from <a href=\"/wiki/House_Jennestas\" title=\"House Jennestas\">House Jennestas</a> infiltrated the city during the 1370s <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>, bringing a large number of dangerous <a href=\"/wiki/Snake\" title=\"Snake\">snakes</a> with them to populate the grasslands surrounding the city. The Jennestas also hid magical effects within the city that attracted the snakes, resulting in a much higher number of fatalities from the serpents' encounters with the citizens.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Rumors_.26_Legends\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rumors_&amp;_Legends\">Rumors &amp; Legends</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Rumors &amp; Legends\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Rumors &amp; Legends\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As series of tunnels beneath the city connected to the <a href=\"/wiki/Pit_of_Vipers\" title=\"Pit of Vipers\">Pit of Vipers</a> temple in the <a href=\"/wiki/Black_Jungles\" title=\"Black Jungles\">Black Jungles</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PaP-p86_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PaP-p86-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Delselar?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRA-p9-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRA-p9_1-2\">1.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Karen_Wynn_Fonstad\" title=\"Karen Wynn Fonstad\">Karen Wynn Fonstad</a> (August 1990). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Forgotten_Realms_Atlas\" title=\"The Forgotten Realms Atlas\">The Forgotten Realms Atlas</a></i>. (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a>), p. 9. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0880388573\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0880388573\">978-0880388573</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRCS3.M-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS3.M_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS3.M_2-1\">2.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Map included in <a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sean_K._Reynolds\" title=\"Sean K. Reynolds\">Sean K. Reynolds</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Skip_Williams\" title=\"Skip Williams\">Skip Williams</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Rob_Heinsoo\" title=\"Rob Heinsoo\">Rob Heinsoo</a> (June 2001). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Setting_3rd_edition\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 3rd edition\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 3rd edition</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>). ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-1836-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-1836-5\">0-7869-1836-5</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-SK-p129-130-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-0\">3.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-1\">3.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-2\">3.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-3\">3.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-SK-p129-130_3-4\">3.4</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Eric_L._Boyd\" title=\"Eric L. Boyd\">Eric L. Boyd</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Darrin_Drader\" title=\"Darrin Drader\">Darrin Drader</a> (July 2004). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Serpent_Kingdoms\" title=\"Serpent Kingdoms\">Serpent Kingdoms</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), pp. 129–130. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-3277-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-3277-5\">0-7869-3277-5</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-PaP-p86-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-PaP-p86_4-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eric_L._Boyd\" title=\"Eric L. Boyd\">Eric L. Boyd</a> (September 1997). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Powers_%26_Pantheons\" title=\"Powers &amp; Pantheons\">Powers &amp; Pantheons</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Julia_Martin\" title=\